From 83678cd10d1a2628aacdcf8b26e68592073e1b53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunrisepeak <speakshen@163.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:36:58 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] [clangd] Completion loads preamble declarations itself
 only in a module importer

With module support on, Sema was made to load the preamble's declarations
for every completion, since the index has no symbols of imported modules.
A file that imports no module has every preamble symbol in the index, as
without module support, and its completions paid for the load for nothing:
in a header-heavy file, about a third of the time each completion took.

The load is now forced only when the file imports modules: the preamble's
file, or the draft as the request sees it. A module imported since the
preamble was built -- typed in the file, or brought in by a header it
includes -- is built for the request alone, and the index knows nothing of
it yet. An import line in the draft answers without a scan; otherwise the
request's own module scan, replayed once for the whole completion, does.
---
 clang-tools-extra/clangd/CodeComplete.cpp     | 58 ++++++++++++++++++-
 .../unittests/PrerequisiteModulesTest.cpp     | 46 +++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 102 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

